# Design

## 1. Topology
Star topology: the Layer 3 switch (`L3-SW`) is the core and the gateway for every VLAN; each department connects to its own access switch. `R1` is the only exit point.


| From | To | Link type | Interfaces |
|---|---|---|---|
| L3-SW | SW1 (IT) | 802.1Q trunk | TODO |
| L3-SW | SW2 (Sales) | 802.1Q trunk | TODO |
| L3-SW | SW3 (Administration) | 802.1Q trunk | TODO |
| L3-SW | SW4 (Management) | 802.1Q trunk | TODO |
| L3-SW | SW5 (Human Resources) | 802.1Q trunk | TODO |
| L3-SW | SW6 (Finance) | 802.1Q trunk | TODO |
| L3-SW | R1 | Routed (L3 port, no switchport) | TODO |
| R1 | INTERNET | Simulated | TODO |
| PCs / servers | Their access switch | Access | TODO |

